# Optional: a qwen2.5vl variant with a bigger baked-in context + output window.
#
# WHY: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible /v1 endpoint IGNORES a per-request num_ctx, so
# raising VISION_NUM_CTX in the env does nothing through it -- the model stays at
# its built-in 4096. Baking the window into the model is the way to actually get a
# bigger context on Ollama.
#
# PREFER TILING FIRST. On a CPU box, splitting the calendar (VISION_CALENDAR_TILES=2)
# is faster and more robust than one huge context -- each request stays small. Use
# this Modelfile only if you'd rather process the whole grid in one shot (slower:
# ~15-25 min/run) or if a tile is still too dense.
#
# Build + use:
#   ollama create qwen2.5vl-cal -f deploy/vps-vision/havasu-qwen-cal.Modelfile
#   # then set VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl-cal in /etc/havasu/havasu-vision.env
#   # and VISION_MAX_TOKENS=8192 to match num_predict.

FROM qwen2.5vl:3b
PARAMETER num_ctx 12288
PARAMETER num_predict 8192
